{
  "$meta": {
    "source": "Five REAL MCP tool results captured read-only from Grom's UK GoHighLevel sub-account on 2026-07-27, then redacted.",
    "redaction": [
      "Every id, email, phone, name, title, note, address, message body, URL and campaign name is SYNTHETIC.",
      "STRUCTURE is byte-faithful: same keys, same key order, same nesting, same JS types, same array lengths, same string forms (ISO-with-millis-Z vs ISO-with-offset vs epoch-millisecond NUMBER).",
      "Instants are mapped one-to-one, so every cross-field invariant the real capture had survives: meta.startAfter === last.sort[0], meta.startAfterId === last.sort[1], conversation sort[0] === lastMessageDate, contact searchAfter[0] === Date.parse(dateAdded), contact searchAfter[1] === its own id.",
      "monetaryValue is synthetic but is still a NUMBER on every row, which is what the live capture showed."
    ],
    "whyItMatters": [
      "structuredContent is the WORKER ENVELOPE {action,status,ok,data,note,filter,pagination,error}; the GHL body is at .data.",
      "action.method is 'POST' for contacts-v3__search-contacts-advanced, which is the exact value that trips kernel.mjs assertSafeCollected. The envelope is kept here ON PURPOSE so the tripwire can be tested."
    ]
  },
